  "description": "Installation of Smart Hub Unit&nbsp;with integrated digital screens&nbsp;",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: Arial, sans-serif; white-space-collapse: preserve;&quot;&gt;The proposed development, by virtue of its scale, design and positioning, is harmful to visual amenity insofar as it would be harmful to the character and appearance of the immediate context; the setting of the Clapton Pond Conservation Area; and the wider streetscene and thus the visual amenity of the area. As such the proposal is contrary policies D3, D4 (Delivering Good Design), D8 (Public Realm) and HC1 (Heritage Conservation and Growth) of the London Plan (2021) and policies PP1 (Public realm), LP1 (Design Quality and Local Character), LP3 (Designated Heritage Assets) and LP7 (Advertisements) of the Hackney Local Plan 2033 (2020). NPPF Paragraph 215.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
